<!--CLI Documentation — Responsibilities
  FQN: com.machineblocks.bml.cli.documentation.Responsibilities-->
<clidoc:Responsibilities xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:clidoc="com.machineblocks.bml.cli.documentation">

  <baseType>
    core:Documentation
  </baseType>
  <is>
    What the host does and what it leaves to other packages
  </is>
  <documentation>
    This host does:

    - Bootstrap a TypeRegistry from @blockml/core (org.blockml.bml.*) plus
      @machineblocks/core (com.machineblocks.bml.*), using the same project
      bootstrap the universal CLI uses.
    - Register the render target before compile. The universal bootstrapTargets
      path is not used for this name. validate does not need the target registry;
      compile does.
    - Pass mbLibPath so generated SCAD can import lib/block.scad and
      config/mb_config.scad from the installed @machineblocks/core (or an
      override path).
    - Default the compile target to machineblocks-v3-scad. The command does not
      take a target name.
    - Resolve the type selector with the framework scan, keep blocks whose
      baseType chain includes Block or Set, and pass the resolved mapping
      (automatic, or sourcePackage plus targetPackage) on targetOptions.
    - Compute every target FQN and output path before writing. One failure
      writes nothing.
    - Write .scad files, preset JSON, and source maps under the configured
      srcDir. The published writer does not enforce that root; this host checks
      the resolved real paths, then calls it with cleaning disabled.

    This host does not:

    - Parse or validate with its own code.
    - Register blockdoc, xsd, or fatblock. Users who need those run blockml.
    - Hardcode MBOM property lists. Those stay in NativeBlock.bml.
    - Ship the SCAD library. That is @machineblocks/core lib/ and blocks/.

    Node.js 20 or newer. The host bin is Node-only. The render target and the
    engine remain browser-capable; only this package may use Node file APIs.

  </documentation>
  <references>
    <see type="clidoc:Commands" relation="ReadNext" />
  </references>
</clidoc:Responsibilities>
